<title>SLOVENIA: Ljubljana bourse changes main SBI stock index.</title>
<headline>Ljubljana bourse changes main SBI stock index.</headline>
<dateline>LJUBLJANA 1997-06-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Ljubljana Stock Exchange said on Friday it had changed the blue-chip SBI index at the beginning of the month to include port operator Luka Koper.</p>
<p>At the same time, it removed pharmaceutical product trader Salus and financial consultancy Nika from the index because of consistently thin trade in the two issues.</p>
<p>The SBI now comprises ten shares -- Luka Koper, drug maker Lek, banks SKB, Probanka and ordinary shares of Dolenjska banka, food makers Droga and Kolinska, health resort operator Terme Catez, shopping centre operator BTC and ordniary shares of trader Kovinotehna.</p>
<p>The bourse said it would revise the index again on September 15.</p>
<p>-- Marja Novak, Ljubljana newsroom, 386-61-125-8439</p>
